    "description": "T17, FR-MD05 and the UX spec's Stale / cached row: a read answered from the read cache is a real answer to the operator and it carries its age, so it is never presented as live data. The resolver joins it to the answer sentence with a single space. The cached value is re-read from the backend on the next read once the backend answers, so no refresh affordance is needed for this release. Neutral register, no tuteo or voseo.",
    "placeholders": {
